{
  "$schema": "../../../../docs/catalog/schema/package.schema.json",
  "id": "Lyo.Diagram.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Diagram.Postgres",
  "area": "Core",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL store for diagram documents. Pages and cells are JSONB behind IDiagramStore.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL + EF Core implementation of [`IDiagramStore`](../Lyo.Diagram.Models/README.md). Each diagram is one row in schema `diagram`, table `diagram`. The `name` column is indexed so a list does not read the cell payload. `document` is jsonb holding the pages and cells.\n\nRegister with `AddPostgresDiagramStore` or `AddPostgresDiagramStoreFromConfiguration`. The configuration section is `PostgresDiagram`. A missing section keeps the declared defaults. The context is an `IDbContextFactory<DiagramDbContext>`, opened per call.",
  "features": [
    "**PostgresDiagramStore.** `IDiagramStore` backed by `IDbContextFactory<DiagramDbContext>`.",
    "**JSONB document.** Pages and cells round-trip through `Lyo.Json` defaults. Id and name stay on the row.",
    "**Name index.** `ix_diagram_name` covers list order. Names are limited to 200 characters."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Registration",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresDiagramStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Database schema",
      "text": "PostgreSQL schema `diagram`. Table `diagram` columns: `id`, `name`, `document` (pages and cells), `created_timestamp`, `updated_timestamp`. Migrations history lives in `__EFMigrationsHistory` in the same schema."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Migrations",
      "text": "At design time set `DIAGRAM_CONNECTION_STRING` and run `dotnet ef migrations add MigrationName --project Core/Diagram/Lyo.Diagram.Postgres --context DiagramDbContext`."
    }
  ],
